From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] Scrollbars go in one step instead of fading out

A scrollbar fades out for 250 ms after it has been shown (themes'
scrollbarFadeDuration). On the device (Test V40) every scroll in Settings
updated the 8 px strip of the scrollbar four more times as it went from
black to white through greys: on e-paper each frame of a fade is a panel
update of its own (docs/design/eink-ui.md, rule 5).

The fade now lasts 1 ms, so the next frame draws the scrollbar gone; it
still shows while the list moves and for the delay after (300 or 400 ms).
Not 0: the fade's two keyframes would then have the same time, and Skia's
SkInterpolator::setKeyFrame refuses the second, leaving whatever the
interpolator held before as the end of the fade.

Theme values only, in every base theme that sets one (Theme, Holo and
Material, dark and light), so framework-res keeps its resource names and the
boot image stays as it is. A view that gets scrollbars without reading the
theme (ViewConfiguration's own 250 ms) still fades; that needs a change to
framework.jar, which the boot image is built from.

--- a/core/res/res/values/themes.xml
+++ b/core/res/res/values/themes.xml
@@ -243,7 +243,7 @@
         <item name="panelMenuListWidth">296dip</item>
 
         <!-- Scrollbar attributes -->
-        <item name="scrollbarFadeDuration">250</item>
+        <item name="scrollbarFadeDuration">1</item>
         <item name="scrollbarDefaultDelayBeforeFade">300</item>
         <item name="scrollbarSize">10dip</item>
         <item name="scrollbarThumbHorizontal">@drawable/scrollbar_handle_horizontal</item>
